e1000: disable EEE on a CE4100 PHY under phylink

The MAC has no LPI support and implements no phylink LPI operations, so
phylink leaves the PHY's default EEE advertisement in place. With EEE
negotiated, an RTL8211E blinks its link LED about once a second while
the link idles, so a link LED offloaded to the PHY does not show the
link state. Disable EEE on the attached PHY.

Author: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c
index 5ea42bd..fe45713 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000/e1000_main.c
@@ -1076,6 +1076,9 @@ static int e1000_phylink_init(struct e1000_adapter *adapter)
 		phylink_destroy(phylink);
 		return err;
 	}
+	/* The MAC has no LPI support */
+	if (adapter->netdev->phydev)
+		phy_disable_eee(adapter->netdev->phydev);
 
 	adapter->phylink = phylink;
 	hw->phylink = true;
